 Sends ICMP echo requests to a host and shows each reply's round-trip
 time, measured with the line clock (one tick, 16 or 20 ms).

 Format:
     PING host [count]

 host is a name (looked up with DNS) or an address a.b.c.d; count is
 the number of requests, 4 if not given.
*Example
     $ PING 192.168.1.1 3
     PING 192.168.1.1
     reply from 192.168.1.1: seq=1 ttl=64 time=16 ms
     reply from 192.168.1.1: seq=2 ttl=64 time=16 ms
     reply from 192.168.1.1: seq=3 ttl=64 time=33 ms
